# The raw request bodies are large and they regenerate on a re-run. The counted
# evidence is committed: summary.json carries the reason item read off the wire,
# and stops.jsonl carries every hook payload.
out/*/requests/

# The pane IS the evidence here — `Stop hook (blocked)` and the `Hooks need
# review` menu are both read straight off it, and each capture is a few KB. The
# repo root ignores `*.log`, so it has to be named back in.
!out/*/codex.log
